1
00:06:42,352 --> 00:06:48,352
Sometimes the adventure of a lifetime becomes life itself.

2
00:13:24,705 --> 00:13:30,705
I Dreamed of Africa is a romance, drama, adventure film directed by Hugh Hudson.

3
00:20:07,058 --> 00:20:13,058
Inspired by the true story of indomitable Kuki Gallmann, the film tells of a beautiful and inquisitive woman who had the courage to escape from her
comfortable yet monotonous life in Italy to start anew in the African wilderness with her son, Emanuele, and her new husband, Paolo.

4
00:26:49,411 --> 00:26:55,411
Gallmann faces great danger there but eventually
becomes a celebrated conservationist.

5
00:33:31,764 --> 00:33:37,764
Kuki Gallmann, played by Kim Basinger.

6
00:40:14,117 --> 00:40:20,117
Paolo Gallmann, played by Vincent Perez.

7
00:46:56,470 --> 00:47:02,470
7-Year-Old Emanuele, played by Liam Aiken.

8
00:53:38,823 --> 00:53:44,823
Declan Fielding, played by Daniel Craig.

9
01:00:21,176 --> 01:00:27,176
Franca, played by Eva Marie Saint.

10
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
Simon, played by Lance Reddick.

11
01:13:45,882 --> 01:13:51,882
I Dreamed of Africa is a 2000 American biographical-drama film
directed by Hugh Hudson, starring Kim Basinger.

12
01:20:28,235 --> 01:20:34,235
It also stars Vincent Perez, Eva Marie Saint, Garrett
Strommen, Liam Aiken and Daniel Craig.

13
01:27:10,588 --> 01:27:16,588
It is based on the autobiographical novel I Dreamed of Africa by Kuki Gallmann, an
Italian writer who moved to Kenya and became involved in conservation.

14
01:33:52,941 --> 01:33:58,941
It was screened in the Un Certain Regard section
at the 2000 Cannes Film Festival.

15
01:40:35,294 --> 01:40:41,294
This film was both a commercial and critical failure.

16
01:47:17,647 --> 01:47:23,647
The tone is emotional.
